  "description": "AN EMPTY TCATBALF: end of file on the very first READ, which is the one branch no seeded row can reach. 1000-TCATBALF-GET-NEXT sees FILE STATUS '10', moves 16 into APPL-RESULT, APPL-EOF is true and :340 moves 'Y' into END-OF-FILE, so PERFORM UNTIL at :188 exits without ever entering its body. Nothing is displayed between the two banner lines - no record image, because :193 is inside the loop - nothing is read from the other four datasets even though all five are opened at :182-186, and SYSTRAN is opened and left with zero rows. The empty input is DECLARED, at its copybook width and naming CVTRA01Y, rather than omitted: an omitted dataset is one the case says nothing about, while an empty one asserts that the program opened a real dataset and reached end of file immediately. The distinction is the whole point of this case.",
